  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fill-and-stroke-styles says:\r\n\r\n> The style can be either a string containing a CSS color, or a CanvasGradient or CanvasPattern object. Invalid values are ignored.\r\n\r\nBut there's no definition of what an invalid value is, and as a result browsers diverge:\r\n\r\nhttps://jsfiddle.net/pcrt7e1o/\r\n\r\nCan we get the spec clarified about whether junk at the end of a CSS color is supposed to be treated as a valid value?",
